# Code owners — a pull request that touches any path below needs an approval
# from one of its owners before it can merge into `dev` (ruleset "Code owner
# review (dev)") or `main` (branch protection). Paths no one owns keep the
# usual flow: no approval required.
#
# Two owners on every line, because GitHub never counts an author's approval
# of their own pull request: with one owner, that owner's own changes could not
# merge at all.

# The plugin runtime and SDK. Plugins run inside this process, so this review
# is the barrier between a plugin and the core (see README, Plugins).
/src/plugins/                @Emanuel250YT @leocagli

# The lint rules that confine plugin code, and the CLI that creates, signs and
# installs plugins. Loosening either one is loosening the boundary, so
# they get the same review as the plugins themselves.
/eslint.config.mjs           @Emanuel250YT @leocagli
/scripts/plugins.ts          @Emanuel250YT @leocagli

# The plugins folder: what support ships preinstalled, signed, to every
# deployment — reviewed like the core.
/plugins/                    @Emanuel250YT @leocagli

# CI decides whether lint and tests gate a merge; a change here could switch
# the checks above off.
/.github/workflows/          @Emanuel250YT @leocagli

# This file: otherwise anyone could remove an owner in the same PR that
# needs their review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS          @Emanuel250YT @leocagli
